{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/761724-unstoppable-force-vs-immovable-object-dogs-and-the-solar-athletics-tree","id":761724,"title":"Unstoppable Force vs. Immovable Object, Dogs and the Solar Athletics Tree","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-09T14:42:41-08:00","id":761724,"title":"Unstoppable Force vs. Immovable Object, Dogs and the Solar Athletics Tree","content":"Dogs have special attack of Harry (3e p 562) which after some conditions says a character cannot disengage.<br /> <br /> Solars have a Charm in Atheltics called Eagle Wing Style which allow them to create disengage actions. I'm sure other Exalts will also have other ways to create Disengage actions.<br /> <br /> I see a few ways to rule this:<br /> <br /> 1.) You're a flying Solar, dogs don't get to hold you back!<br /> 2.) UFvIO, you would have a roll off (probably the same rolls as the Disengage Action) to see if you even get the chance to Disengage. Then you would roll again to see if you are successful. <br /> 3.) Dog's got you down.<br /> <br /> Any opinions? This hasn't come up in play, I'm just trying to sort out rulings in advance and while I'm leaning UFvIO on this one I'd be happy to hear from you knowledgeable forumites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T14:46:38-08:00","id":761732,"title":"","content":"I would probably go with number two, though I haven't specifically read those entries yet.<br /> <br /> Edit: After reading them I would still go with 2. Because as best I can tell with Eagle-Wing Style it's a jump and thus uses the same legs that Harry targets to keep you from disengaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","user":"Bulshock","date":". 11-09-2015, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T14:51:08-08:00","id":761734,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure the rule was that in cases like this, the better stunt wins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T14:55:24-08:00","id":761739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/761724-unstoppable-force-vs-immovable-object-dogs-and-the-solar-athletics-tree?p=761734#post761734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure the rule was that in cases like this, the better stunt wins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 189 has that as the rule when players tie on Opposed Actions.<br /> <br /> In this case, the rules are preventing the Opposed Action in the first place, which makes the stunt awkward to phrase. &quot;I attempt to fly off the ground and avoid the dog's yapping jaws, but maybe I'm not allowed to if the dog is narratively cool enough to keep me down.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T14:58:12-08:00","id":761742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/761724-unstoppable-force-vs-immovable-object-dogs-and-the-solar-athletics-tree?p=761739#post761739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 189 has that as the rule when players tie on Opposed Actions.<br /> <br /> In this case, the rules are preventing the Opposed Action in the first place, which makes the stunt awkward to phrase. &quot;I attempt to fly off the ground and avoid the dog's yapping jaws, but maybe I'm not allowed to if the dog is narratively cool enough to keep me down.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, sorry, I still don't have everything down. My bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T15:07:28-08:00","id":761752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/761724-unstoppable-force-vs-immovable-object-dogs-and-the-solar-athletics-tree?p=761742#post761742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, sorry, I still don't have everything down. My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, no harm no foul. Neither do I, it's why I made the thread.<br /> <br /> Also, thanks for the edit, Bulshock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":".  Edit regarding Bulshock's edit 11-09-2015, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T15:36:22-08:00","id":761766,"title":"","content":"Harry prevents disengage. Unless Eagle Wing Style states its disengage cannot be prevented, dogs got you down. They are also not opposed roles, is the affect of a special attack, you resist by not getting hit or only taking 4 withering damage. UFvIO does not enter into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T15:39:17-08:00","id":761769,"title":"","content":"This is solved by looking at the mechanics and asking what they're modeling.<br /> <br /> Harry represents a dog's ability to bite into an ankle or leg and keep the person from running away from the dog. Eagle Wing Style allows you to run off/jump away in a burst of speed.<br /> <br /> The question then is: Will jumping really high or running really fast help you disengage from a pit-bull that has clamped down on your leg?<br /> <br /> The answer here is 'no.' It's biting on your leg. If you want to disengage from it, you need to get if off your leg, not run away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 11-09-2015, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:10:10-08:00","id":761801,"title":"","content":"Gallus, Eagle Wing Style states it allows disengage actions in impossible situations (midair) but does not specifically state that those disengage actions cannot be prevented, But this was never a requirement of UFvIO, just something that was a feature of HGD and SSE - perfect stealth didn't have to be told it protected against perfect identification, that was always clearly a rolloff because ones says you can't hide and the other says you can't see me (Like Invisible Statue Spirit vs. Eye of the Unconquered Sun). There is a similar conflict here regarding movement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/761724-unstoppable-force-vs-immovable-object-dogs-and-the-solar-athletics-tree?p=761769#post761769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is solved by looking at the mechanics and asking what they're modeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what got me here in the first place. Because Harry is specifically boosting a withering attack I've modeled it as a dog that will bite you if you get near it, distracting you and messing up your footwork - not a dog that has actually achieved biting you (which would make more sense for a decisive attack).<br /> <br /> This still puts me in the 'maybe the Solar's fast enough to jump out of the way with some crazy flying magic that can make disengage actions happen in midair, maybe they aren't' conceptual area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:14:56-08:00","id":761806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/761724-unstoppable-force-vs-immovable-object-dogs-and-the-solar-athletics-tree?p=761801#post761801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what got me here in the first place. Because Harry is specifically boosting a withering attack I've modeled it as a dog that will bite you if you get near it, distracting you and messing up your footwork - not a dog that has actually achieved biting you (which would make more sense for a decisive attack).<br /> <br /> This still puts me in the 'maybe the Solar's fast enough to jump out of the way with some crazy flying magic that can make disengage actions happen in midair, maybe they aren't' conceptual area.</div> </div> </div> </div>In action movies, a dog on your ankle is a mild inconvenience - very unlikely to actually tear up your tendons like a real-life dog might do.<br /> <br /> I'd rule that you can jump as high as you want, but the dog is still attached. However, you might be able to survive the fall better than the dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:18:23-08:00","id":761809,"title":"","content":"There's no ambiguity in the rules. Eagle Wing Style allows disengaging in some specific situations where disengages wouldn't be allowed, but having a dog hanging onto your leg isn't one of them. Therefore, you can't disengage with it if a dog has prevented your disengage. You might want to ask your ST to allow a disengage anyway, using your flight powers as a justification for that, but that's a case of changing the rules because it would be cooler/more realistic, not any sort of ambiguity in the rules themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:20:30-08:00","id":761811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/761724-unstoppable-force-vs-immovable-object-dogs-and-the-solar-athletics-tree?p=761766#post761766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harry prevents disengage. Unless Eagle Wing Style states its disengage cannot be prevented, dogs got you down. They are also not opposed roles, is the affect of a special attack, you resist by not getting hit or only taking 4 withering damage. UFvIO does not enter into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the correct way to read that interaction, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:24:37-08:00","id":761814,"title":"","content":"K, thanks for the input, everybody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}